  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Caci NSS obligated $288M in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. Caci NSS won 75 awards so far, with an average award size of $3.8M, and obligations fell 36.0% year over year. Caci NSS received most funding from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $116M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $90.1M and the Department of Defense with $70.3M. Caci NSS saw most of its FY2026 obligations land in Other Computer Related Services, which received $219M, and Computer Systems Design Services, which received $69.1M. Caci NSS has moved through a multi-year rise in obligations from $199M in FY21 to a peak of $449M in FY25 and then to $288M in FY26. Caci NSS current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. Caci NSS’s top buying agencies and top markets show a heavy concentration in Homeland Security and in computer-related services, which explains the large share of obligations in those categories this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How are Caci NSS's FY2026 obligations distributed across agencies?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $116M to Caci NSS in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $90.1M and the Department of Defense obligated $70.3M. Remaining agencies each account for much smaller shares, including the Department of Justice with $4.5M and the Department of Agriculture with $3.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has Caci NSS's funding trended since FY21?",
        "body": "Caci NSS obligations rose from $199M in FY21 to $449M in FY25, then fell to $288M in FY26. Caci NSS obligations fell 36.0% year over year into FY26. Caci NSS FY2026 totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial."
      }
    ]
  },
